{
  "version": "4.9.1-beta.4",
  "changelog": {
    "Improvements": [
      "**Transactional frozen updates (PC):** Frozen Windows updates now use isolated per-attempt staging directories and kernel-level exclusive file locking (`update_frozen_install.lock`), cleanly rejecting conflicting concurrent updates without file corruption.",
      "**Literal argument preservation:** Arguments are safely transported via structured JSON and passed directly through Win32 `CreateProcessW`, preserving spaces, quotes, `%PATH%`, ampersands, and Unicode without batch interpolation or environment expansion vulnerabilities.",
      "**Immutable generations & staged activation (Android):** Android Python runtime updates are placed into versioned, immutable generation directories (`generations/gen_<timestamp>`). Live sessions remain pinned to their active generation while new updates are staged cleanly (`vX.Y.Z staged`) until the next application restart.",
      "**Target version selection (PC & Android):** Pick and switch to any release version directly from the GUI on both PC (Preset Editor sidebar) and Android (Python Engine card), with full preset and data safety."
    ]
  },
